                    <msContents>
                        <summary>
                            
                            <p>This is built in at the beginning of lines and is also incomplete. It is a verse inscription in characters of about the 13th century A.D. It seems to be in praise of some merchant community whose members made name and money in such cities as Vāruṇāpati, Vellūr Nellūr, Kāñchī, Pūmpugār, Paḻaiyārai and Teṉ-Madurāpuri. It refers to a gift of lamp to god Śiva at Madurai (Māṉēndiya-Karamuḍai-Marudar).</p>						
                            
                        </summary>
                    </msContents>
